  "passage": "Last Friday, our school's geography club organised a special assembly about Antarctica, the world's most remote continent. Mr. Brown, a teacher with a passion for polar regions, gave a typical presentation that captivated the audience. He explained that a minute in Antarctica's extreme weather can feel much longer, and shared stories of his past expeditions. During the question time, students were encouraged to ask questions immediately after each segment. Many queries were similar to those from previous years, showing a lasting interest in the topic. To raise awareness and funds, the school also sold a product: a set of postcards and a calendar featuring stunning Antarctic photos. The items sold out quickly, and the proceeds will go to an environmental charity. The assembly was not only educational but also inspired many students to learn more about our planet's fragile ecosystems.",
